 ["Harshavardhana ruled north India from Kannauj in the 7th century. The Chinese traveller Xuanzang visited his court.","In the south, the Pallavas ruled from Kanchipuram. King Narasimhavarman built the rock-cut temples and monolithic rathas at Mamallapuram.","Their art and architecture influenced the later Chola temples."],
